# Vocabulary versions covered by conformance fixtures in this repo.
# Compare against spec/VOCAB_VERSIONS to detect drift.
# Run scripts/check-downstream-versions.sh from spec/ to check all repos at once.
# Update this file when adding new fixture categories for a vocabulary version.
#
# WHAT A ROW HERE CLAIMS (tightened 2026-08-03, when the fixtures were executed
# by automation for the first time and several rows turned out to be unbacked):
# a version row means at least one fixture instantiates a class that a shape in
# that vocabulary targets, and `scripts/run_conformance.py` evaluates a non-zero
# number of constraints against it. It is a claim of exercised coverage, not of
# mere compatibility, and it is checkable by running the suite. Where a version
# introduced something no fixture reaches, the gap is named rather than implied.
#
# The shapes the suite actually runs against come from the revision named in
# scripts/SPEC_PIN, not from this file. If the two disagree, SPEC_PIN wins and
# the rows below describe a vocabulary CI is not executing, so keep them in step:
# SPEC_PIN's `vocab=` line must repeat the versions below verbatim. As of
# 2026-08-28 both read core=3.7 health=2.8 clinical=1.16 coverage=1.6
# coverage=1.6: cascade:AIExtracted joins InsurancePlanShape dataProvenance
#   (every clinical/health shape had it since clinical v1.9; this was the miss).
#   AI-extracted InsurancePlan fixture tracked upstream, not yet here.
# checkup=3.3 pots=1.4, and the pin is the spec PR #31 merge commit 678ae0d
# (tags vocab/core-v3.7, vocab/health-v2.8, vocab/clinical-v1.16,
# vocab/coverage-v1.5, all four on that commit).
#
# 2026-08-27 batch: core 3.7 / health 2.8 / clinical 1.16 / coverage 1.5
# (spec PR the-cascade-protocol/spec#31, merge commit 678ae0d; tags
# vocab/core-v3.7, vocab/health-v2.8, vocab/clinical-v1.16, vocab/coverage-v1.5,
# all four on that same commit). 25 fixtures added across four directories, 24
# of which pass; the 25th is a defect this batch FOUND in the release and is
# enumerated in KNOWN_FAILURES.json under ownedBy "spec" (see below). Suite goes
# 109/136 to 133/161. The pre-existing 136 score identically at both pins,
# fixture for fixture and reason for reason, which is the release's "additive and
# strictly widening" claim measured rather than quoted.
#
# A THIRD FIXTURE POLARITY EXISTS AS OF THIS BATCH. Five of this release's
# rulings are sh:Warning bindings, per the ratchet core v3.5 wrote down: a value
# existing data already carries is REPORTED, never rejected. A two-polarity
# runner cannot assert that -- .INVALID.ttl fails such a fixture with
# NO_VIOLATION and .VALID.ttl passes it while asserting nothing -- so
# `<slug>.WARN.ttl` was added, meaning "at least one sh:Warning AND no
# sh:Violation". It is strictly an added assertion and cannot turn a failing
# fixture into a passing one. Three new mutation tests in
# scripts/selftest_runner.py hold it up, and all three were observed RED against
# a deliberately neutered runner before being committed.
#
# THE DEFECT FOUND: clinical v1.16 says all five clinical:status bindings are
# sh:Warning. That holds on clinical:ClinicalDocumentShape and fails on every
# class reaching it through sh:node, because SHACL defines conformance as an
# EMPTY result set, so a nested sh:Warning makes the value node non-conforming
# and the outer sh:node constraint reports a sh:Violation at its own default
# severity. All six document subtypes are affected, for
# clinical:documentReferenceStatus as well as clinical:status. Reproduced on two
# independent engines (pyshacl 0.30.1 and cascade-cli 0.17.0). The fixture
# clinical/status-laboratoryreport-in-progress.WARN.ttl asserts what the release
# SAYS and is baselined until spec fixes the severity.
#
# 2026-08-08 batch: health 2.6 / clinical 1.14 / coverage 1.4 / checkup 3.3.
# Shapes-only alignment to ratified standards (spec PR the-cascade-protocol/spec#16).
# Five fixtures added, and one KNOWN_FAILURES entry removed rather than re-explained:
